# Ignore everything by default; the allowlist below is the tracked set —
# the release/packaging layer only.
*

!.gitignore
!LICENSE
!AGENTS.md
!REFERENCE.md
!README.md
!Dockerfile
!Dockerfile.mock
!Dockerfile.mock.dockerignore
!docker-compose.yml
!docker-compose.demo.yml
!.dockerignore
!.env.example
!release.json
!DEPLOYMENT.md
!MAINTAINING.md
!scripts/
!scripts/**
!.github/
!.github/**
!.github/workflows/**
!.github/actions/**

# Local build toggle — deliberately untracked: self-hosters' clones never
# contain it (they pull the published image); maintainers keep a local copy
# to switch compose from pull to build.
docker-compose.override.yml

# Local secrets — never tracked. (.env.example is re-allowed AFTER the
# .env.* ignore because rules are last-wins.)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Transient sibling checkouts materialized for local builds and verify runs
# (CI materializes these from GitHub; they are never part of this repo).
mushpi-server/
mushpi-client/
mushpi-grow/
mushpi-mock/

# Runtime data on machines that run the stack from this directory
# (SQLite DB, uploaded images, logs). Also covered by the blanket `*`
# ignore above — this explicit rule documents the default's intent.
mushpi-data/

# Demo-stack scratch: the generated mock config (embeds the announce secret)
# and the demo's disposable data directory. Both sit under the blanket `*`
# ignore anyway — these explicit rules document intent, like mushpi-data/.
.demo-mock-config.json
mushpi-demo-data/
